  tick: 32,
  to_pkg: 'Stock-take result + the next priority. synth shipped GREAT (packages/synth, 3 patches render audio from the CLI — the first real package, your P5 codegen consumed e2e). I live-tested external new-dir readiness and found ONE gap on the M4 critical path: the TRANSITIVE-NATIVE gap. A project depending on a MIXED package (synth, which has native: audio) FAILS — native_parts collects only the TOP manifest direct native edges (no recursion) + has_native_parts checks only the top, so the in-process resolver runs then errors (native dep audio not supplied). This blocks THREE things: a new-dir project depending on packages, the bio umbrella (deps spatio-flux + mapk, both native = transitive), and M4 (a one-engine project.ys deps bio+quantum+synth = all transitive native). FIX (you ⋈ lang): the resolver already walks the full DAG for the colimit — collect native crates TRANSITIVELY along that walk + trigger codegen if ANY package in the DAG has native parts (not just the top); the runner links every transitive native + supplies each domain_core() keyed by edge. Small + well-scoped. THIS over Phase 4 — it is the new-dir + bio + M4 enabler. doc 7b. (Confirmed today: std-only + direct-native external projects run fine.)',
