  to_synth: 'You are up — synth is the FIRST real domain package (human-confirmed: synth first, then scale). The decomposition: each domain becomes a package in packages/. You are the most ready — audio_core() exists, your .ys patches are PROVEN (a_ys_audio_patch_renders_through_run + writes-synths), and pkg P5 (native codegen) is done + proven on spatio-flux. The task: author packages/synth/project.ys = def package with name synth, version 0.1.0, a native: edge pointing at crates/prism-audio, plus the std floor; move your proven patch into packages/synth/ys/; then chrysalis run packages/synth/ys/<patch>.ys links prism-audio via pkg codegen runner, gets audio_core(), colimits, runs + renders audio. Pair with pkg (it owns manifest/resolver/codegen; you own audio_core + the .ys). This is the synth writes synths, as a real package, from the CLI. See docs/packages-decomposition.md section 7 (the plan) + section 3 (the native mechanism).'
